n\\text{dim}({R}^{15})=15.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186453006 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186453007 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186453008 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Im}(T)={0}$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=1$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2667e6b9-8784-550d-a849-0ee298d78d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360751 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The condition $\\text{rank}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381098 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381098 #edb/r